PRETABLE 20 -- written 2026-10-16 BEFORE table 20 runs (its own file; this mtime orders table 20 alone).
Instrument: probe v24 (m88k_exc_probe_v24.FROZEN.py, md5 a035efeb...) = v23 + repair 15, the is_trap axis (Fable 5.1, pass 15):
m88k_exception() TESTS four inputs -- vector, PSR & SFRZ (:811), cpu->delay_slot (:840, :865) and is_trap (:816) -- so the floor
is {7 labels} x {SFRZ} x {delay_slot} x {is_trap}: 56 cells, 8 unreachable (is_trap 0 at BOUNDS and ERROR: no non-trap raise
site names 7 or 10 -- tcnd/tb0/tb1 are the only is_trap=1 sites and the only routes into 7/10), 48 reachable, 38 rowed by v23.
v24 adds the 10 open cells (a TRAP in a slot at MISALIGN, UNIMPL, PRIV, DIV0, OVF -- unfrozen dslot<L>tb, frozen
trapfrozen<L>dslot) and one clause-(e) row, sfu1hdslot (the fallback at SFRZ set in a slot).  84 fault rows.  Base HEAD 7b23b785.

DISCLOSED, clause (e), measured below as escapes: the user-trap labels (128 / 0x1c2 / MVMEPROM_VECTOR / default) x {slot}
-- outside the fix's seven labels; their delivery predates #502 (trapfrozen128/450/496/511 were voluntary closures of the
exemption's label range); {delay slot} x {MODE, SER, C, SFD1, IND} (copied or ORed, never tested); vectors 0..3's own
delay-slot code (upstream, m88kexchwtraps).

CHANNEL per new row and the mutant it kills:
  dslot<L>tb (five)         M_ARMTSU_<L> (`implemented = !(delay_slot && is_trap && !(PSR & SFRZ))' at L): HALT replaces DELIVER
  trapfrozen<L>dslot (five) M_RRDS_<L> (`!is_trap || (vector == L && delay_slot)' at :816): re-routed to 0x50 -> STOP
  sfu1hdslot                M_FBFRZDS (`&& !(delay_slot && (PSR & SFRZ))' at :799): no halt -> re-routed / delivered, not HALT

